{"id": "q0409", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 3.01, "n_chunks": 4, "scores": [0.4748, 0.4155, 0.3716, 0.4154], "eot_score": 0.9302, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used ?", "transcript": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The \"Philly Special\" was a famous trick play run by the Philadelphia Eagles in Super Bowl LII against the New England Patriots. It was used on February 4, 2018, near the end of the first half on 4th-and-goal. Eagles quarterback Nick Foles lined up as if he were changing the play, the ball was snapped directly to running back Corey Clement, handed to tight end Trey Burton, and Burton threw a touchdown pass to Foles. The play helped the Eagles win 41–33, giving them their first Super Bowl title.", "expert_answer": "The **Philly Special** was a famous trick play run by the **Philadelphia Eagles** in **Super Bowl LII** against the **New England Patriots**.\n\nIt was used on **February 4, 2018**, near the end of the **first half**, on **4th-and-goal**. Eagles quarterback **Nick Foles** lined up as if he were changing the play, the ball was snapped directly to running back **Corey Clement**, handed to tight end **Trey Burton**, and Burton threw a touchdown pass to Foles.\n\nThe play helped the Eagles win **41–33**, giving them their first Super Bowl title.", "expert_latency_s": 5.34, "stall_ms": 30, "relay_ms": 3791}
{"id": "q0421", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 4.21, "n_chunks": 5, "scores": [0.4123, 0.3847, 0.2428, 0.2656, 0.3457], "eot_score": 0.2336, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "transcript": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "mode": "local", "answer": "Swinging a golf iron and a golf driver are similar in fundamentals but differ significantly in technique due to the clubs' design and intended use. Here's a breakdown of the best way to swing each, with key differences highlighted for optimal performance with both clubs, especially when comparing irons versus drivers from an instructional standpoint like in *Golf with Common Sense! Irons vs. Drivers – How They're Different! Golf Instructional Videos! Golf Tips!* by Golfingwithsense.com, which emphasizes smart techniques over brute force and common misconceptions about power generation through the body or grip strength alone—though such factors can play supporting roles if used correctly within proper mechanics and timing considerations such as those detailed in resources like Golf Tips for Beginners and How to Play Golf on Golfingwithsense.com or even broader sports training insights shared across platforms like Quora and Reddit's golf communities where users discuss nuances of club selection and swing dynamics including how clubs vary based on distance covered during a typical round of golf or equipment choices made per individual player preferences shaped by their skill level development stages starting from early teen years through adulthood with consistent practice routines informed by expert advice available online via channels dedicated to improving one's game through smart, sustainable techniques rather than relying solely on exaggerated movements that may lead to injury or inconsistency over time—such as focusing too much on \"how do i play golf\" without understanding the underlying principles of efficient energy transfer between body segments during impact phases crucial for both driver and iron shots alike as explained in depth within instructional materials targeting learners at all levels seeking improvement through evidence-based guidance rather than myths perpetuated by less credible sources.", "answer_ms": 10631}
{"id": "q0426", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 2.9, "n_chunks": 3, "scores": [0.4051, 0.3532, 0.3358], "eot_score": 0.2399, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "transcript": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The purpose of a shot clock in basketball is to ensure that the game maintains a steady pace and prevents teams from holding the ball for extended periods without attempting a shot. The shot clock, typically set at 24 seconds in professional leagues like the NBA, gives a team only a limited amount of time to attempt a field goal after gaining possession of the ball. This rule encourages offensive movement, faster gameplay, and more scoring opportunities overall. It helps prevent stalling tactics and keeps the game dynamic and engaging for players and spectators alike.", "answer_ms": 3241}
